@startuml Cohesion Examples

' Title
title Cohesion Examples - From Weakest to Strongest

' Hide package names to focus on classes
hide circle
hide empty members

' Style settings
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<Coincidental>> LightGray
  BackgroundColor<<Logical>> LightBlue
  BackgroundColor<<Temporal>> LightGreen
  BackgroundColor<<Procedural>> LightYellow
  BackgroundColor<<Communicational>> LightPink
  BackgroundColor<<Sequential>> LightSalmon
  BackgroundColor<<Functional>> LightCyan
  BorderColor Black
  ArrowColor Black
}

' Coincidental Cohesion (Weakest)
class CoincidentalCohesion <<Coincidental>> {
  + generateRandomId()
  + convertToUpperCase()
  + factorial()
  + isLeapYear()
  + formatDeal()
  + validateEmail()
  + calculateCircleArea()
  + reverseString()
}
note bottom of CoincidentalCohesion
  <b>Coincidental Cohesion</b>
  Weakest form of cohesion.
  Methods are grouped arbitrarily
  with no meaningful relationship.
end note

' Logical Cohesion
class LogicalCohesion <<Logical>> {
  + validateUser()
  + validateDeal()
  + validateDealProduct()
  + validateCommissionRate()
  + validateDealProducts()
  + validateDealStatusTransition()
}
note bottom of LogicalCohesion
  <b>Logical Cohesion</b>
  Methods perform similar functions
  (validation) but on different
  types of data.
end note

' Temporal Cohesion
class TemporalCohesion <<Temporal>> {
  - users
  - deals
  - commissionCalculations
  + processDealClosed()
  - updateDealStatus()
  - setDealCloseDate()
  - calculateCommission()
  - notifySalesRep()
  - notifySalesManager()
  - notifyFinanceTeam()
  - updateSalesReport()
  - updateCommissionReport()
  - updateRevenueForecasts()
  - logDealClosedActivity()
}
note bottom of TemporalCohesion
  <b>Temporal Cohesion</b>
  Methods are executed at the
  same time (when a deal is closed)
  but perform different functions.
end note

' Procedural Cohesion
class ProceduralCohesion <<Procedural>> {
  + createDeal()
  - validateInputs()
  - createBasicDeal()
  - addProductsToDeal()
  - calculateDealValue()
  - setDefaultDates()
  - assignUniqueId()
  - logDealCreation()
}
note bottom of ProceduralCohesion
  <b>Procedural Cohesion</b>
  Methods follow a specified
  sequence of execution in
  the deal creation process.
end note

' Communicational Cohesion
class CommunicationalCohesion <<Communicational>> {
  + analyzeDeal()
  - calculateDealMetrics()
  - isDealProfitable()
  - isDealAtRisk()
  - generateDealSummary()
  - isEligibleForSpecialDiscount()
  - calculateExpectedCloseDate()
}
note bottom of CommunicationalCohesion
  <b>Communicational Cohesion</b>
  Methods operate on the same
  data (Deal object) but perform
  different operations.
end note

' Sequential Cohesion
class SequentialCohesion <<Sequential>> {
  + calculateCommission()
  - extractEligibleProducts()
  - calculateBaseCommissionAmount()
  - determineCommissionRate()
  - applyCommissionRate()
  - calculateBonusAmount()
  - calculateFinalCommissionAmount()
  - createCommissionCalculation()
}
note bottom of SequentialCohesion
  <b>Sequential Cohesion</b>
  Output from one method becomes
  input to another, forming a
  data processing chain.
end note

' Functional Cohesion (Strongest)
class FunctionalCohesion <<Functional>> {
  + calculateDealValueWithDiscounts()
  - calculateBaseValue()
  - calculateVolumeDiscount()
  - calculateMultiProductDiscount()
  - calculateEarlyPaymentDiscount()
  - calculateTotalDiscount()
  - applyDiscount()
  + calculateDiscountPercentage()
  + isDealEligibleForDiscounts()
}
note bottom of FunctionalCohesion
  <b>Functional Cohesion</b>
  Strongest form of cohesion.
  All methods contribute to a
  single, well-defined task.
end note

' Model classes used by the cohesion examples
class Deal {
  - id
  - title
  - value
  - status
  - salesRepId
  - products
  - closeDate
  - createdDate
  - lastModifiedDate
  + calculateTotalValue()
}

class DealProduct {
  - id
  - productId
  - productName
  - quantity
  - price
  - discount
  - dealId
  + calculateTotalPrice()
}

class User {
  - id
  - username
  - email
  - firstName
  - lastName
  - roles
  + getFullName()
  + isSalesRep()
}

class CommissionCalculation {
  - id
  - dealId
  - salesRepId
  - baseCommission
  - bonuses
  - accelerators
  - grossCommission
  - netCommission
  - status
  + calculateTotalCommission()
  + recalculate()
}

enum DealStatus {
  OPEN
  WON
  LOST
  CANCELLED
}

' Relationships
CoincidentalCohesion ..> Deal : uses
LogicalCohesion ..> User : validates
LogicalCohesion ..> Deal : validates
LogicalCohesion ..> DealProduct : validates
LogicalCohesion ..> DealStatus : validates
TemporalCohesion --> Deal : processes
TemporalCohesion --> User : uses
TemporalCohesion --> CommissionCalculation : creates
ProceduralCohesion --> Deal : creates
ProceduralCohesion ..> User : uses
ProceduralCohesion ..> DealProduct : adds to deal
CommunicationalCohesion ..> Deal : analyzes
CommunicationalCohesion ..> DealProduct : uses
CommunicationalCohesion ..> DealStatus : checks
SequentialCohesion ..> Deal : processes
SequentialCohesion ..> User : uses
SequentialCohesion ..> DealProduct : processes
SequentialCohesion --> CommissionCalculation : creates
FunctionalCohesion ..> Deal : calculates value
FunctionalCohesion ..> DealProduct : uses
FunctionalCohesion ..> DealStatus : checks

' Cohesion strength scale
note "Cohesion Strength Scale (Weakest to Strongest)" as N1
note "1. Coincidental Cohesion" as N2
note "2. Logical Cohesion" as N3
note "3. Temporal Cohesion" as N4
note "4. Procedural Cohesion" as N5
note "5. Communicational Cohesion" as N6
note "6. Sequential Cohesion" as N7
note "7. Functional Cohesion" as N8

N1 .. N2
N2 .. N3
N3 .. N4
N4 .. N5
N5 .. N6
N6 .. N7
N7 .. N8

@enduml